    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Turkic dynasty, probably of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karluks">Karluk</a> origin, that ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balasagun">Balasagun</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a> from the mid-9th century.</li><li>The first Turkic state to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a> in 999, bringing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> under Turkic rule.</li><li>Its court culture gave rise to the first works of Turkic Islamic literature; rivalry split it in two around 1042.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Mahmud al-Kashgari, a prince of the Kara-Khanid dynasty, drew a round map of the world with the Turkic lands at its centre for his dictionary of the Turkic languages.</p></aside>
    </section>

